-- MIKO --> Focus point inside a bookmarked page (C15).
-- Fraction (0..1) of the bookmarked page's height where the user's attention was when the
-- bookmark was created: the long-pressed point for the reader's long-press sheet, the centre of
-- the viewport for the top-bar toggle. It is what the Favorites thumbnail and the page preview
-- centre on. `scroll_fraction` (52.sqm) keeps meaning "top edge of the viewport" and is still
-- what reopening the reader restores; the two are deliberately separate.
-- NULL means "unknown": every bookmark made before this migration, and every bookmark made in a
-- paged reading mode. Those fall back to the scroll_fraction band, then to the image centre.
-- DDL kept byte-identical to page_bookmarks.sq.
ALTER TABLE page_bookmarks ADD COLUMN focus_fraction REAL;
-- MIKO <--
